 "about_text": "FOYER-LA is an artist-run exhibition space in Los Angeles, founded in 2019 by artist Connie Walsh. Set behind a courtyard in front of Walsh's own studio, it describes itself as an in-between space for experimentation, dialogue, and collaboration. Since opening, the gallery has presented more than thirty projects, ranging from solo debuts to conceptually driven installations across sculpture, drawing, and performance. Its program has included artists such as Ellie Krakow, Michael Ashkin, Ana Maria Devis, and James Rose, alongside Walsh's own work. The space favors small-scale, provocative shows that explore themes of intimacy, transition, and the body, positioning itself as a laboratory for experimentation rather than a conventional commercial gallery.",
